    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #243\n\n- 2026-09-17 03:29Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-17 04:20Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #420 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-243-operations-01-08-enforce-runtime-datab-thr_bv4j84uzpd`. ## Summary Implements issue #243: least-privilege runtime Postgres roles and per-service connection strings. - **Migration `backend/packages/data/src/db/migrations/0039_least_privilege_roles.sql`**: creates `semprec_data` (full DML on the 9 choke-point tables) and `semprec_side` (SELECT-only on choke-point tables, full DML on all 38 module side tables and all public-schema sequences), with `semprec_data` granted membership in `semprec_side` so it can complete generic transactions that also touch side tables (e.g. the blob-plus-item transaction in `fileUploadStore.ts`). - **`grantQueueSchemaPrivileges`** (`backend/packages/queue/src/index.ts`): grants `semprec_side` access to graphile-worker's `graphile_worker` schema, including explicit RLS policies for its four RLS-enabled private tables (graphile-worker enables RLS but ships no policies, so plain GRANTs alone don't unblock DML). - **Service configuration**: `semprec-api/.env.example` documents the `semprec_data` connection string (it's the one service hosting the choke-point); `semprec-ai-gateway/.env.example` documents `semprec_side`. - **Tests**: `leastPrivilegeRoles.test.ts` (integration, 6 tests against a real Postgres instance) verifies all three acceptance criteria plus queue access and a sequence-backed side-table insert; `serviceRoleConfig.unit.test.ts` verifies no service outside `semprec-api` documents `semprec_data`. - **Docs**: `docs/operations/database-roles.md` describes the role model and per-service assignment. Full `pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, unit, migration numbering, write-safety/boundary checks, integration, e2e) passes clean. 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-17 04:50Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #420 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-243-operations-01-08-enforce-runtime-datab-thr_bv4j84uzpd` (confirmed: `origin` now points at `8fbc9ac`, matching local `HEAD`). ## Enforce runtime database roles and least-privilege service connections (issue #243) Adds two least-privilege Postgres roles for runtime service connections: - **`semprec_data`** — full DML on the choke-point tables only (`databases`, `properties`, `relation_definitions`, `items`, `item_relations`, `views`, `view_items`, `idempotency_keys`, `rollup_dependencies`). Used by `semprec-api`, the only service hosting the generic choke-point. Inherits `semprec_side` so it can also complete side-table writes started in the same transaction/process. - **`semprec_side`** — read-only (`SELECT`) on the choke-point tables, full DML on every module side table and sequence, and full access to the queue (`graphile_worker` schema, including RLS policies for its policy-less private tables). Used by every other service (e.g. `semprec-ai-gateway`), so a bug that tries to bypass the choke-point from one of those services is rejected by Postgres itself. This update to the pull request fixes the CI failure reported on run [35181563862](https://github.com/dvdtrsnk/semprec/actions/runs/35181563862/job/105074631088): 1. **Migration ordinal collision**: a `develop` merge brought in `0039_observability_checks.sql`, colliding with this branch's own `0039_least_privilege_roles.sql`. Renumbered to `0040_least_privilege_roles.sql` and added the newly merged-in `observability_checks` table to `semprec_side`'s grant list. 2. **Queue grant wiring gap** (independently confirmed by acceptance-criteria review): `ensureQueueSchema`/`grantQueueSchemaPrivileges` were only invoked from the test `globalSetup.ts`, never from `runMigrationsCli.ts` (the real-deploy entrypoint), so `semprec_side` would never receive `graphile_worker` schema privileges outside of tests. Wired both calls into `runMigrationsCli.ts`, matching the `app-code-post-migration-steps` ADR's dual-invocation rule. Verified with `pnpm run verify` in both `backend/` (lint, format, build, unit/integration/e2e tests) and `web/` (lint, format, build, tests) — all green. 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-17 05:32Z — This issue was resolved by #420, which just merged into develop.",
